            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="1107" n="971" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg971"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/975: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-17T16:00:00-06:00">November 17, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>112. Your telegram No. 82, November 12, 5 p.m. In a note dated November 16 the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs requests me to inform the Department that his
                    “Government’s delegation will be ready January next.”</p>
                <p>Repeated to Guatemala.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
